  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find the value of $f(x)=x{e}^{\u2308x+0.6\u2309}$ at $x=1.2.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.",
  "worked_solution": "Suppose that $x$ is a real number. The least integer (or ceiling) function $\u2308x\u2309$ equals the smallest integer that is greater than or equal to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\u2308x\u2309=n,\\,\\text{where}\\,n-1<x\\le n,\\,n\\in Z\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(x)$ at $x=1.2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.2) & =1.2{e}^{\u23081.2+0.6\u2309} \\\\  & =1.2{e}^{\u23081.8\u2309}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the definition of the least integer function, we have\n\n$$\n\u23081.8\u2309=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.2) & =1.2{e}^{\u23081.8\u2309} \\\\  & =1.2{e}^{2} \\\\  & =1.2(7.389\\,05\u2026) \\\\  & =8.866\\,86\u2026 \\\\  & \u22488.87,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
